WEBVTT

00:07:28.621 --> 00:07:32.704
and dictionaries are the documents
that chronicle that language use.

00:07:33.413 --> 00:07:35.163
Here's one example.

00:07:35.204 --> 00:07:37.204
We currently use the word "awful"

00:07:37.246 --> 00:07:41.329
to talk about something
that is bad or gross.

00:07:42.038 --> 00:07:45.996
But before the 19th century,
"awful" meant just the opposite.

00:07:46.454 --> 00:07:48.704
People used "awful" to talk
about something

00:07:48.746 --> 00:07:50.538
that was deserving of respect

00:07:50.579 --> 00:07:52.538
or full of awe.

00:07:54.079 --> 00:07:55.871
And in the mid-1900s,

00:07:55.871 --> 00:07:59.121
"awesome" was the word
that took up these positive meanings

00:07:59.163 --> 00:08:02.246
and "awful" switched
to the negative one we have today.